course: dictionary
lesson: 13743
title: Interbreed: when different kinds have young together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To interbreed means that animals or plants of different kinds, breeds or groups mate and have young together. The word has two parts: inter means between, and breed means to have young, so interbreed means having young between groups.
explain: Use the context to check. «The farmer's horse and donkey interbred, and their young was a mule.» The horse and donkey had young together, so interbred must mean mated and had young together. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The horse and donkey mated and had young together, and their young was a mule." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Scientists look at whether animals can interbreed and have young that can have young too. Members of the same species usually can. Different species usually cannot, or their young cannot have young of their own. A mule is one example of this.
fact: Interbreed means for different kinds, breeds or groups to mate and have young together.
fact: Interbreed is a verb: interbreed, interbreeds, interbred, interbreeding.
fact: «Interbred» is the past tense: «The two plants interbred last spring.»
fact: Scientists define a species partly by whether its members can interbreed and have young that can have young too.
fact: «Early modern humans and Neanderthals interbred», so many people today carry a little Neanderthal DNA.
exercise: «The horse and the donkey interbred, and their young was a mule.» What does interbred mean? | *Mated and had young together | Grew very tall | Were sold at the market | Ran away from each other
exercise: Which word is the past tense of interbreed? | interbreeding | *interbred | interbreeds
exercise: Scientists say a horse and a donkey are different species. What does that suggest about their young? | They always look the same as their parents | They cannot eat grass | *They usually cannot have young that can have young too | They are always very strong
test: «Many people today carry a little Neanderthal DNA because our ancestors interbred.» What does interbred mean here? | Fought each other for food | Grew old quickly | Moved to a new country | *Mated and had young together
test: Which pair are members of the same species and can interbreed? | A cat and a fish | *Two grey squirrels | A lion and a bird | A horse and a donkey
exam: Mia says «interbreed» is just another word for «fight». Is she right? | *No, interbreed means to mate and have young together | Yes, it means to run away from danger | Partly, it means to argue about who is in charge | Yes, it means to fight over food
